## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple port of `SmallMultiplesChart` (web → SwiftUI + Swift Charts) as **10 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/SmallMultiplesChart.*`, following the established `ChartLegend`/`ChartContainer` shared-surface architecture.

**Parity reproduced from the web source:**
- Verbatim ports of the three web perf layers: `isFinitePoint`, `strideSample`, and per-cell finite-only projection.
- Per-cell own y-scale (the whole point of small multiples), responsive grid (web `auto-fill minmax` → `LazyVGrid`, whose lazy row build is the native peer of the web `IntersectionObserver` lazy-mount), shared time-cursor crosshair (web `syncId` peer via `chartXSelection` + `RuleMark`), and the per-cell **"No data"** branch using the one verbatim web key `smallMultiples.noData`.
- All states render: loading / error / empty / populated + stale/offline freshness. Bound through the P1/S8 state-holder seam, emits the P1/S11 `view.opened` event, all copy via the P1/S10 facade. VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, Reduce Motion. Unit + projection + model + view tests and per-state previews included.

**Verification (real results):**
| Step | Result |
|---|---|
| swiftlint --strict (9 files) | **0** |
| swiftformat --lint (9 files) | **0** |
| placeholder gate | **0** |
